.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
plugin that creates a file-info 'tooltip' 

this plugin creates tooltips that are centered around the item the tooltip is for.
.PP
some tunables exist as defines and should be turned into properties at some point. ###
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "static \fBicon_el\fP* frame_new (Evas * evas, \fBicon\fP * icon, \fBicon_el\fP * el, double x1, double y1, double x2, double y2, int state)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
create a frame around the tooltip. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
a linked list of icon-elements. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIevas\fP - the evas 
.br
\fIicon\fP - the tooltip to append the elements to (needed by ICON_EL_*()) 
.br
\fIel\fP - the current icon-element 
.br
\fIx1\fP - left boundary 
.br
\fIy1\fP - upper boundary 
.br
\fIx2\fP - right boundary 
.br
\fIy2\fP - lower boundary 
.br
\fIstate\fP - state mask for the icon-elements to create
.RE
.PP

.SS "void tt_dst (void ** data)"
.PP
destruct a tooltip. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIdata\fP - the tooltip-handle \fBtt_new()\fP gave us
.RE
.PP

.SS "void* tt_new (void * data, int x, int y, \fBfile_info\fP * fi)"
.PP
create a tooltip. 
.PP
no assumptions about the nature of the tooltip are made; for all the main application knows, the plugin might read the info to the user aloud.
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
a handle to pass to \fBtt_dst()\fP when destroy the tooltip. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIdata\fP - the icon-list the tooltip is related to 
.br
\fIx\fP - x-position of the icon the info is for 
.br
\fIy\fP - y-position of the icon the info is for 
.br
\fIfi\fP - the file we're displaying info for
.RE
.PP

